WEBVTT

﻿1

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:11.639
Hey, I've been doing some homework


00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:13.839
on this kid Tobey Marshall
from Mount Kisco.


00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:17.199
This kid was a phenom. Used to
tear up the local circuits.


00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:20.519
Him and his dad, man, they
campaigned like champions.


00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:22.999
Of course, Mount Kisco had
another great, Dino Brewster.


00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.199
You all know Dino.


00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:25.879
He went on to race in
the big leagues at Indy


00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:29.119
and Tobey just kind of
fell through the cracks.


00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:31.439
Well, here's some news, cretins.


00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:34.439
Tobey's been running
again, and running fast.


00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:38.199
Real fast, fast as that "Grim
Taquito" will take him.


00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.839
Tobey, you wanna fly
with the eagles,


00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:43.799
you need bigger wings, son.


00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:45.239
I'm just telling you right now


00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:49.519
that if Tobey Marshall ever got
a car worthy of his talents,


00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:52.644
he could be toeing
the line at De Leon.


00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:57.199
Give me four clicks of compression.


00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.731
All right.


00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:01.242
Actually, make it three.


00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.239
No, two. Two is perfect.


00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:09.159
You wanna make up your mind?
What is it, two, three, or four?


00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:10.839
- Exactly.
- Yo, guys!


00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:12.119
You know I'm gonna hurt you, right?


00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:13.599
- Two.
- Thank you.


00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.039
Guys. Joe, you gotta
check this out, man.


00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:17.924
- Yo.
- Monarch's on fire.


00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:19.239
Cretin, go ahead.


00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:21.239
Monarch, this is Darryl
from East Orange.


00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.959
Why would you let a redneck trust
fund baby into the De Leon?


00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:26.399
He doesn't deserve to be
in a winner-takes-all race


00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.119
with multi-million-dollar cars!


00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:29.441
- Come on, Monarch!
- Caller?


00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:31.291
Do I get to talk?


00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:34.879
Darryl, have your parents ever
smacked you upside the head?


00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:37.759
See, this is a case where sometimes
you just need to beat kids.


00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:40.199
Darryl, Darryl,
it's my show. I get...


00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.919
Shut up! Listen to me!


00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:43.359
Darryl, one important question.


00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:45.599
Have you ever even
driven a race car?


00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.370
That's what I thought.


00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:51.730
Let me explain to all of you people out
there how this works one more time.


00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:54.559
It's my race.


00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:57.439
It's the De Leon. I created it.


00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:00.079
It's rarefied air, kids.
It's beautiful.


00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:01.639
I decide who gets in,


00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:04.399
and who does not get
in to the race, okay?


00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.439
I loved your dad.


00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:09.759
He was a customer of
the bank for 30 years.


00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:11.200
Thirty.


00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:13.279
What y'all talking about?


00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:15.399
The Flyin' Hawaiian just
took down Steve Heavy Chevy


00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:16.886
- in the Arizona desert.
- What?


00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:26.959
An invitation as a wild card.
Okay? That's important.


00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:28.799
Wild card. Maybe.


00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:31.765
I'm not saying he's in,
I'm saying he might be.


00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:34.365
Who was that?


00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:37.685
He's just an old
customer of my dad's.


00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:40.045
I didn't recognize him.


00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:43.919
Yeah, he might bring
his car in on Friday.


00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:45.479
What's wrong with it?


00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:47.045
Our job to find out.


00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:49.799
I was thinking about the race tonight.
We should get there early.


00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:52.759
Five cars, the race is full.
Pot should be, like, what?


00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:54.405
Five grand.


00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:52.088
- Tobey.
- Pete.


00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:54.039
- You good?
- Good.


00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:55.679
- Are you ready?
- Yeah.


00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:58.519
You know, Monarch
gave you a shout-out.


00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:01.199
- Then he shit on your car.
- Yeah, I know. I heard.


00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.319
Never mind that.


00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:04.841
While Monarch was talking
about you, I had a vision.


00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:06.199
All right, here we go.


00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.559
Quiet, okay? I happen
to like his visions.


00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:09.807
Pete, proceed, please.


00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:13.839
I see water, and the sun, and...


00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:16.239
- Your sister in a bikini.
- Shut it.


00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:19.250
I see Tobey looking
at a lighthouse.


00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:23.039
I see you, and you're
gonna win De Leon.


00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:24.159
- Really?
- Hey.


00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:26.039
Thanks for the vote
of confidence, Petey,


00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:27.399
but I got my hands full


00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:31.810
trying to beat Jimmy Macintosh
and you tonight, so...


00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:38.804
Oh, man.


00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:42.519
My sister and Dino are here.


00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:43.919
She didn't tell me she
was coming home, Tobe.


00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:45.770
I'm sorry.


00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:49.406
No, it's fine.


00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:51.924
Coming with Dino isn't.


00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:54.043
What's this fool even
doing back here, man?


00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:57.449
Maybe he just came to watch
how a real racer drives.


00:05:57.880 --> 00:05:59.239
The guy raced Indy.


00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:02.489
It doesn't get more
real than that, Finn.


00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:07.799
Let's go, Tobey. You don't
need that distraction.


00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.039
No, it's fine.


00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:11.119
All right, boys, the race
is gonna start soon.


00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:12.959
Ben, you should head up.


00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:15.959
I just wanna let you know
I'm going because I want to


00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:17.679
and not because you told me to.


00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:19.439
- Just know that.
- Okay.


00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:21.005
Way to put your foot down, Benny.


00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:23.479
Nice pleather jacket, homie.


00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:25.439
- Hey.
- Hi, guys. Hi, Petey.


00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:26.559
How are you?


00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:28.079
- I'm good. How are you?
- Good.


00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:30.679
- Are you racing tonight?
- Yeah.


00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:32.359
- You be careful.
- Okay.


00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:33.721
Okay.


00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:41.399
Hi, Tobey.


00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:43.329
Anita.


00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:46.326
I'm really sorry to
hear about your dad.


00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:51.369
Did you get my flowers?


00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:53.045
Yeah.


00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:55.681
Good.


00:06:57.280 --> 00:06:59.403
And thank you for
watching out for Pete.


00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:03.368
He's like a little brother to me.


00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:05.361
How's the shop?


00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:08.599
The shop is... It's good.


00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:09.847
It's good.


00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:13.247
Yeah?


00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:15.689
How's the city?


00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:19.799
It's different than I expected,


00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:22.810
but it's not here.


00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:29.526
Are you still allergic
to Mount Kisco?


00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:33.719
Actually, Dino has something
he wants to talk to you about.


00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:35.039
I doubt that.


00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:38.210
After the race, though.
I don't wanna distract you.


00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:42.324
Then you should have
stayed in Manhattan.


00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:47.249
You look beautiful.


00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:00.247
- How are you feeling?
- Good.


00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:01.879
Have you got the roads locked down?


00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:03.279
The road is clear.


00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:06.131
We are at the finish line
and Benny is in the Cessna.


00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:10.519
Liar One, you standing by?


00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:12.239
Here we go with this again.


00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:13.399
I wouldn't have to use that handle


00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:15.759
if you stopped telling people
you flew Apache helicopters.


00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:17.679
I took an Apache for
a joyride, okay?


00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:18.919
That's all I said.


00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:21.079
I know that's what you said.
We just don't believe you.


00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:24.439
Hey, man, look, just because I'm a crew
chief doesn't mean I don't know how to fly.


00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:27.599
You gotta have balls of
titanium alloy to do what I do.


00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:31.771
So I need a little respect.
A little R-E-S-P-E-C-T.


00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:34.399
All right, enough messing
around. What's the status,


00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:35.919
Liar One?


00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:37.451
Clear, and this is "Maverick."


00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:39.399
Call me Maverick,


00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:41.921
or I will kamikaze this
into your nut sack.


00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:04.969
Mind if I watch?


00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:42.239
Okay, gentlemen,
please be advised,


00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:43.919
I got traffic ahead.


00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:46.009
Repeat, I got traffic ahead.


00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:10.528
That was close. He got lucky.


00:11:10.880 --> 00:11:13.651
It's not luck. He's patient.


00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:43.567
Sorry, little buddy.


00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:14.764
My house!


00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:20.081
Benny!


00:13:20.160 --> 00:13:23.250
You bodied that guy's grocery cart.


00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:25.249
What's wrong with you?


00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:51.601
Yeah!


00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:17.810
Yeah!


00:14:20.600 --> 00:14:22.962
Sweet!


00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:26.399
Hey, yo, Father Joseph, make
sure you save me a beer, buddy.


00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:28.090
Hello?


00:14:31.960 --> 00:14:33.571
That's what we do. That's right.


00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:35.679
Benny, my man.


00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:36.959
I thought you had him, brother.


00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:39.239
Nah, I had him in the turns.


00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:40.999
Where were you? We missed
you, brother, we missed you.


00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:42.159
What do you mean?


00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:43.279
I was flying, watching your butts.


00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:44.839
- You were flying?
- Flying?


00:14:44.840 --> 00:14:47.639
- I didn't see him flying.
- Y'all gonna play me like that?


00:14:47.640 --> 00:14:49.359
- I didn't see him flying.
- Did you see him flying?


00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:51.319
Maybe you should ask
the shopping cart guy


00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:52.720
if he saw you flying up there.


00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:55.679
Shots fired! Boom, boom!


00:14:55.680 --> 00:14:57.279
So I'm supposed to
watch out for cops,


00:14:57.280 --> 00:14:59.239
fly the plane, make sure
you got a clear lane


00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:01.199
and look out for homeless people
coming out of the shadows?


00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:03.084
I didn't get that memo, I'm sorry.


00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:21.091
Nice driving.


00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:24.364
I'm impressed.


00:15:25.120 --> 00:15:27.049
Tobey Marshall.


00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:30.606
The man to beat in Mount Kisco.


00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:36.687
Sorry about your old man.


00:15:38.520 --> 00:15:40.879
I know you were close.


00:15:40.880 --> 00:15:44.243
You lost, Dino?


00:15:44.480 --> 00:15:45.920
What?


00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:48.359
I mean, I haven't seen you
around for a long time.


00:15:48.360 --> 00:15:50.961
I figured, you know,
you must be lost.


00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:54.402
So, nothing has changed.


00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:58.404
After 10 years, you wanna just
pick up some locker room fight.


00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:00.719
What do you want?


00:16:00.720 --> 00:16:02.759
I wanna see you build a real car.


00:16:02.760 --> 00:16:05.804
I got plenty of cars
to build, Dino.


00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:08.051
Yeah.


00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:10.011
How's that going for you?


00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:13.925
I didn't come to insult you.


00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:16.765
I came to make a
business proposition.


00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:20.079
It could be a game-changer for you.


00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:22.079
Are you handing out
dreams now, Dino?


00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:26.285
I've seen a hundred custom racing
shops since I left this town.


00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:29.129
I still haven't seen
work as good as yours.


00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:32.879
That's these guys. Not me.


00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:35.279
I have a very special car
that needs to be finished.


00:16:35.280 --> 00:16:36.879
What kind of car are
we talking about?


00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:38.650
Ford Mustang.


00:16:39.400 --> 00:16:40.601
A Mustang?


00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:46.689
It's the one Ford and Carroll Shelby
were building when Carroll died.


00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:49.399
How did you get it?


00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:51.728
Mr. Shelby and my
uncle, they were close.


00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:55.567
You finish building my Mustang
like you rebuilt that Gran Torino,


00:16:57.040 --> 00:16:59.759
I'll give you a quarter of
what we get for the car.


00:16:59.760 --> 00:17:01.439
A quarter?


00:17:01.440 --> 00:17:03.449
The car is worth 2 million.


00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:05.166
Minimum.


00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:07.284
That's $500,000 in your pocket.


00:17:10.120 --> 00:17:12.971
Forget about the past, Tobey.


00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:15.809
It's history.


00:17:17.560 --> 00:17:20.161
I'm here to make peace.


00:17:20.440 --> 00:17:22.608
And money.


00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:25.930
Don't answer me now.


00:17:26.240 --> 00:17:28.408
Just think about it.


00:17:30.800 --> 00:17:33.162
I don't need to think about it.


00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:37.163
I'll do it.


00:17:37.600 --> 00:17:40.531
I'll get the car here tomorrow.


00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:58.522
Okay, I just wanna be the first to
take the floor here and ask you...


00:17:58.960 --> 00:18:01.159
Have you lost your mind?


00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:03.239
You're gonna have us
work for Dino Brewster?


00:18:03.240 --> 00:18:04.519
Word?


00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:06.079
What are you thinking, Tobey?


00:18:06.080 --> 00:18:08.199
You don't wanna have anything
to do with that piece of shit.


00:18:08.200 --> 00:18:11.639
And, look, if this is about Anita,
trying to get her back or something...


00:18:11.640 --> 00:18:13.239
Do it another way, homie.


00:18:13.240 --> 00:18:15.519
Write a poem or some shit. Okay?


00:18:15.520 --> 00:18:16.919
I'll help you out.


00:18:16.920 --> 00:18:20.999
"Dear Anita, Nothing
is sweeter than Anita


00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:24.010
"I really aneeda... Anita"


00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:27.279
And I just came up
with that just now.


00:18:27.280 --> 00:18:28.720
Just now!


00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:32.641
Yo, forget about that
fool and his turtleneck.


00:18:32.920 --> 00:18:34.639
All right? Just tell
him you're out.


00:18:34.640 --> 00:18:36.879
We're doing fine without him.


00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:38.491
We're not.


00:18:42.480 --> 00:18:45.763
Okay. We're not doing fine.


00:18:53.040 --> 00:18:54.810
Look...


00:18:56.200 --> 00:19:00.610
I'm behind on the loan.


00:19:01.680 --> 00:19:03.959
That guy from earlier...


00:19:03.960 --> 00:19:06.359
That guy is from the bank.


00:19:06.360 --> 00:19:10.007
And he's just gonna
keep coming back.


00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:15.128
Tobey, if you say we need him,


00:19:16.440 --> 00:19:18.369
then I'm with you.


00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:23.959
Wait. We made five grand tonight.


00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:26.199
It's gotta be enough
to make the payment.


00:19:26.200 --> 00:19:27.599
What about next month?


00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:29.131
We'll figure it out.


00:19:29.720 --> 00:19:31.679
We always do.


00:19:31.680 --> 00:19:34.247
This time it's different, okay?


00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:41.879
If you guys don't show up tomorrow


00:19:41.880 --> 00:19:43.570
to work on that car,


00:19:45.400 --> 00:19:47.329
we're gonna lose this place.


00:19:52.200 --> 00:19:53.879
Hey, come on, guys.


00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:55.366
This is Carroll Shelby.


00:19:55.720 --> 00:19:57.888
This is an opportunity
of a lifetime.


00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:02.402
We're doing this.
All right? For Tobey.


00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:05.002
9:30 tomorrow. Don't be late.


00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:13.239
You're cheating, man.
Quit cheating!


00:20:13.240 --> 00:20:14.959
You just can't keep up.


00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:16.446
Shit!


00:20:18.080 --> 00:20:19.691
Here we go.


00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:28.919
Yeah.


00:20:28.920 --> 00:20:30.724
All right, all right, all right.


00:20:36.480 --> 00:20:38.523
Where is the rest of it?


00:20:38.720 --> 00:20:40.999
We got a lot of work to do.


00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:42.247
Yeah.


00:22:05.240 --> 00:22:06.799
Do you like that car over there?


00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:08.764
- Yeah, it's nice.
- Yeah.


00:22:09.080 --> 00:22:10.919
We built that.


00:22:10.920 --> 00:22:14.442
So, you're a mechanic.


00:22:16.920 --> 00:22:18.759
That was real smooth, bro.


00:22:18.760 --> 00:22:21.645
Hey. Do you like
that car over there?


00:22:21.920 --> 00:22:23.759
Okay. Excuse me.


00:22:23.760 --> 00:22:25.644
We built that.


00:22:26.240 --> 00:22:28.479
We're mechanics.


00:22:28.480 --> 00:22:31.650
We're not afraid to
get our hands dirty.


00:22:32.600 --> 00:22:35.326
Do you know what I mean?


00:22:36.720 --> 00:22:38.604
Do you like that car over there?


00:22:55.280 --> 00:22:57.323
How fast does it go?


00:22:58.840 --> 00:23:00.279
Fast.


00:23:00.280 --> 00:23:02.084
Very fast. Pete.


00:23:02.280 --> 00:23:04.528
Aren't all Mustangs fast?


00:23:04.800 --> 00:23:08.799
Well, this one was built by Ford
and reimagined by Carroll Shelby,


00:23:08.800 --> 00:23:11.519
the greatest performance car
builder in American history.


00:23:11.520 --> 00:23:13.559
She's not from around here, Petey,


00:23:13.560 --> 00:23:18.004
so she probably has no idea
who Carroll Shelby is.


00:23:18.640 --> 00:23:20.639
But why is it so fast?


00:23:20.640 --> 00:23:23.446
It's 900 horsepower, baby.


00:23:23.800 --> 00:23:25.445
Is that a lot?


00:23:26.200 --> 00:23:28.079
- Are you kidding me?
- Petey.


00:23:28.080 --> 00:23:31.363
Look, miss, this isn't the kind of car
you can just go to the mall and buy.


00:23:31.480 --> 00:23:33.523
Trust me when I say,
it's one of a kind.


00:23:36.320 --> 00:23:38.045
Can I see the engine?


00:23:40.040 --> 00:23:41.446
Sure.


00:23:53.000 --> 00:23:55.487
5.8 liter, aluminum block,


00:23:55.600 --> 00:23:59.725
SVT supercharger
and racing headers.


00:24:00.560 --> 00:24:02.888
Yeah, it's quite nice, actually.


00:24:06.760 --> 00:24:08.279
I wasn't expecting that.


00:24:08.280 --> 00:24:10.279
Nor was I.


00:24:10.280 --> 00:24:11.599
Why?


00:24:11.600 --> 00:24:14.087
Because I'm a woman?
Or because I'm from England?


00:24:14.720 --> 00:24:19.439
Mr. Shelby's first Cobra was built
using an AC body made in England.


00:24:19.440 --> 00:24:22.559
It had a Ford 260 CID V8 engine.


00:24:22.560 --> 00:24:24.285
Of course, you already knew that.


00:24:24.800 --> 00:24:27.207
Life can be full of surprises.


00:24:30.880 --> 00:24:32.919
I find life to be full of
people who think they're smart


00:24:32.920 --> 00:24:34.999
because they have a fancy accent.


00:24:35.000 --> 00:24:36.201
No offense.


00:24:36.320 --> 00:24:37.760
Some taken.


00:24:39.920 --> 00:24:42.282
I really love Piers Morgan.


00:24:42.880 --> 00:24:44.079
So, this is how it goes, is it?


00:24:44.080 --> 00:24:45.719
You're very quiet, very tough,


00:24:45.720 --> 00:24:49.322
and then you're just constantly
cracking these hilarious jokes.


00:24:49.960 --> 00:24:51.650
Hey, Jules.


00:24:53.800 --> 00:24:55.679
Three million is way too
much for this car, Dino.


00:24:55.680 --> 00:24:57.609
Well, that's what it costs.


00:24:57.800 --> 00:25:00.399
- Let's see what Ingram thinks.
- I am what Ingram thinks,


00:25:00.400 --> 00:25:02.039
and he thinks two at the most.


00:25:02.040 --> 00:25:03.287
Well, three is the number.


00:25:03.520 --> 00:25:05.640
Three is absurd. That's
why nobody has bid on it.


00:25:05.760 --> 00:25:08.159
That's the best car
I've driven since Indy.


00:25:08.160 --> 00:25:11.011
You haven't driven it, Dino. Tobey's
had the keys the whole time.


00:25:14.760 --> 00:25:16.599
Do you want me to turn
around and plug my ears


00:25:16.600 --> 00:25:18.564
while you all get on the same page?


00:25:19.120 --> 00:25:20.199
What's the top speed?


00:25:20.200 --> 00:25:21.599
- 180.
- 230.


00:25:21.600 --> 00:25:22.759
230?


00:25:22.760 --> 00:25:24.803
He's talking about a
theoretical top speed.


00:25:25.360 --> 00:25:26.679
I know that you don't really talk,


00:25:26.680 --> 00:25:29.804
but maybe Mr. Strong and Silent
could be a little less silent.


00:25:30.480 --> 00:25:32.119
She'll go 230.


00:25:32.120 --> 00:25:34.239
Top NASCAR speed ever was 228.


00:25:34.240 --> 00:25:35.646
This car is faster.


00:25:43.440 --> 00:25:45.359
8:00 a.m., tomorrow at Shepperton.


00:25:45.360 --> 00:25:47.319
You get anything close
to 230 out of this car,


00:25:47.320 --> 00:25:49.039
Ingram is going to
buy it on the spot.


00:25:49.040 --> 00:25:50.399
For 3 million.


00:25:50.400 --> 00:25:52.204
Give or take a million.


00:25:53.000 --> 00:25:54.850
Mostly take.


00:25:55.680 --> 00:25:57.086
Good night, lads.


00:25:58.960 --> 00:26:00.241
Bye.


00:26:02.680 --> 00:26:03.959
230?


00:26:03.960 --> 00:26:06.208
Are you crazy? What if I
can't get the car there?


00:26:06.320 --> 00:26:09.199
Well, maybe you can't,


00:26:09.200 --> 00:26:11.926
but I can.


00:26:12.000 --> 00:26:13.406
I'll drive.


00:26:14.000 --> 00:26:16.680
Don't even think about
driving that car.


00:26:47.960 --> 00:26:49.730
Yeah, Tobey!


00:27:01.080 --> 00:27:03.647
What are you guys doing?


00:27:04.080 --> 00:27:07.011
Stop! Stop!


00:27:10.480 --> 00:27:11.920
What the hell are you doing?


00:27:12.440 --> 00:27:15.639
You don't own this car!
You don't get to joyride it!


00:27:15.640 --> 00:27:17.919
Top speed just over 230.


00:27:17.920 --> 00:27:19.690
234.


00:27:20.720 --> 00:27:22.968
According to this.


00:27:23.400 --> 00:27:24.761
Hey.


00:27:27.400 --> 00:27:28.806
That was some driving, son.


00:27:29.640 --> 00:27:31.808
And that is one hell of a car.


00:27:32.560 --> 00:27:34.808
It's going to cost me $3 million?


00:27:35.080 --> 00:27:36.611
That's the price.


00:27:37.160 --> 00:27:39.647
2.7.


00:27:52.960 --> 00:27:55.447
2.7 million?


00:27:57.120 --> 00:27:59.607
What the hell were you thinking?


00:27:59.760 --> 00:28:02.327
We sold the car, Dino.


00:28:03.440 --> 00:28:06.723
You never could've got that
car to 230. Even on our track.


00:28:06.840 --> 00:28:08.690
You think you're a
better driver than me?


00:28:11.120 --> 00:28:13.448
Everyone knows he's
a better driver.


00:28:14.320 --> 00:28:15.759
You know, I'm just about
done with you, Pete.


00:28:15.760 --> 00:28:18.439
Hey! Back off, Dino.


00:28:18.440 --> 00:28:20.679
I'll beat you on a track, the dirt,


00:28:20.680 --> 00:28:22.799
a road, anywhere
else you wanna race.


00:28:22.800 --> 00:28:25.319
Hey, you're the man, okay?


00:28:25.320 --> 00:28:26.399
You're the pro.


00:28:26.400 --> 00:28:27.879
You got nothing to prove
to me. Let's move on.


00:28:27.880 --> 00:28:29.039
No.


00:28:29.040 --> 00:28:30.439
No, let's race.


00:28:30.440 --> 00:28:34.199
If you win, I'll give you
my 75% of the Mustang deal.


00:28:34.200 --> 00:28:36.209
If you lose,


00:28:36.640 --> 00:28:39.207
you give me your 25%.


00:28:44.120 --> 00:28:46.004
Well, that makes it interesting.


00:28:56.800 --> 00:28:59.048
This is the biggest house
I've ever seen.


00:28:59.160 --> 00:29:01.319
It's my uncle's place.


00:29:01.320 --> 00:29:04.046
Don't worry, he's in Monaco.


00:29:04.560 --> 00:29:06.683
These aren't even legal
in the United States.


00:29:07.080 --> 00:29:08.479
They're all Euro-spec cars,


00:29:08.480 --> 00:29:10.360
so technically, they
don't even exist here.


00:29:11.040 --> 00:29:13.083
Are they some kind of Ferrari?


00:29:13.160 --> 00:29:14.999
Koenigsegg Agera R.


00:29:15.000 --> 00:29:18.363
Top speed, 270 miles an hour.


00:29:19.000 --> 00:29:21.931
But, Dino, I thought you
didn't go faster than 180.


00:29:24.360 --> 00:29:26.403
You got a big mouth for a fan.


00:29:26.840 --> 00:29:29.199
Yeah, well, then let me race.


00:29:29.200 --> 00:29:30.999
I'll be happy to have you, Pete.


00:29:31.000 --> 00:29:32.884
- Awesome. I'm in.
- Whoa, whoa, whoa.


00:29:32.920 --> 00:29:34.399
Hey. Sit this one out.


00:29:34.400 --> 00:29:36.602
No. Let him be a big boy.


00:29:39.080 --> 00:29:41.719
Three identical Ageras.


00:29:41.720 --> 00:29:43.001
After you.


00:29:52.120 --> 00:29:56.079
The finish line is at the end
of the bridge, over the 684.


00:29:56.080 --> 00:29:58.760
The first car to get to
the other side wins.


00:30:07.560 --> 00:30:09.091
Tobey.


00:30:13.560 --> 00:30:15.524
This is my vision.


00:30:16.080 --> 00:30:18.079
This is how I saw you
winning De Leon.


00:30:18.080 --> 00:30:21.170
You beat Dino, take
his car and win.


00:30:41.800 --> 00:30:43.161
Wow.


00:32:29.680 --> 00:32:30.881
Whoa!


00:32:59.880 --> 00:33:01.684
Thanks, little buddy!


00:33:03.000 --> 00:33:04.281
You got it, man!


00:33:08.200 --> 00:33:09.561
Yeah, Pete.


00:33:26.520 --> 00:33:27.721
Come on!


00:33:29.120 --> 00:33:31.209
We got him, Pete.


00:34:23.400 --> 00:34:24.601
No!


00:34:31.720 --> 00:34:34.571
No, no, no, no, no.


00:34:56.280 --> 00:34:57.561
Pete!


00:35:01.280 --> 00:35:03.005
No!


00:35:24.400 --> 00:35:25.931
No!


00:35:48.880 --> 00:35:52.479
"Fear not, for I am with you.


00:35:52.480 --> 00:35:55.559
"Be not dismayed,
for I am your God.


00:35:55.560 --> 00:35:58.239
"Behold, all those who
were incensed against you


00:35:58.240 --> 00:36:00.761
"shall be ashamed and disgraced.


00:36:01.240 --> 00:36:03.399
"They shall be nothing.


00:36:03.400 --> 00:36:07.959
"Those who war against
you shall be as nothing.


00:36:07.960 --> 00:36:11.239
"For I shall hold your
right hand, saying to you,


00:36:11.240 --> 00:36:15.445
"'Fear not, I will help you."'


00:36:16.480 --> 00:36:20.119
Let's go through this
again, Mr. Marshall.


00:36:20.120 --> 00:36:23.599
A couple witnesses say they
may have seen three cars,


00:36:23.600 --> 00:36:26.804
but we can't find the third car.


00:36:28.600 --> 00:36:30.599
Why don't you use that
diagram there to show us


00:36:30.600 --> 00:36:32.882
where you claim the
third car to have been.


00:36:38.480 --> 00:36:43.004
My car was about two
car lengths ahead.


00:36:45.000 --> 00:36:50.439
This is where Pete was,
and Dino was right behind him.


00:36:50.440 --> 00:36:54.879
He tapped his back bumper
hard, and at an angle.


00:36:54.880 --> 00:36:58.050
Dino has two witnesses who say
they were with him the whole day.


00:36:58.640 --> 00:37:01.079
And the owner of Brewster Motors


00:37:01.080 --> 00:37:04.170
reported two Koenigseggs
stolen last week.


00:37:05.720 --> 00:37:10.005
Just seven minutes before police
arrived at the scene of the crash.


00:37:10.240 --> 00:37:12.999
That's his uncle, okay?


00:37:13.000 --> 00:37:16.044
They're lying.


00:37:17.600 --> 00:37:21.088
All right? He was there.


00:37:22.800 --> 00:37:25.446
Dino was there.


00:37:26.880 --> 00:37:28.650
Mr. Marshall,


00:37:29.760 --> 00:37:33.203
you're the only one that can
place Dino at the scene.


00:37:36.360 --> 00:37:39.131
No way is this happening.


00:37:39.720 --> 00:37:41.604
This isn't happening.


00:37:42.520 --> 00:37:45.121
Pete... This isn't happening.


00:38:08.000 --> 00:38:09.519
- Bill Ingram speaking.
- Sign here.


00:38:09.520 --> 00:38:11.719
Mr. Ingram, Tobey Marshall.


00:38:11.720 --> 00:38:14.241
I need to borrow your
Mustang to race De Leon.


00:38:16.880 --> 00:38:19.208
Excuse me, son?


00:38:19.280 --> 00:38:21.839
You want to race my
Mustang in De Leon?


00:38:21.840 --> 00:38:23.199
What's in it for me?


00:38:23.200 --> 00:38:25.801
When I win, I will give
you half the cars.


00:38:27.000 --> 00:38:30.090
That's around $4 million for you.


00:38:30.920 --> 00:38:32.839
I'll think about it.


00:38:32.840 --> 00:38:34.679
I'll call Julia.


00:38:34.680 --> 00:38:37.087
All right. Step forward.
Go. Everybody.


00:38:44.480 --> 00:38:46.559
Come on. Come to me.


00:38:46.560 --> 00:38:48.119
That's my boy.


00:38:48.120 --> 00:38:49.199
Is Joe in?


00:38:49.200 --> 00:38:50.639
Already on the road with the Beast.


00:38:50.640 --> 00:38:52.759
If this thing works, we're
gonna need that head start.


00:38:52.760 --> 00:38:54.079
What about Finn?


00:38:54.080 --> 00:38:57.519
We haven't convinced him
yet, but we will. It's Finn.


00:38:57.520 --> 00:38:59.439
But more importantly, do
we even have a vehicle?


00:38:59.440 --> 00:39:01.722
I'll know in an hour.


00:40:07.720 --> 00:40:10.839
Hey, thanks for dropping it off.


00:40:10.840 --> 00:40:14.123
And thank Ingram for me, please.


00:40:14.680 --> 00:40:16.159
So, what do you think?


00:40:16.160 --> 00:40:18.079
First American car to win De Leon?


00:40:18.080 --> 00:40:19.359
Definitely.


00:40:19.360 --> 00:40:21.562
You don't even have an invite.


00:40:23.760 --> 00:40:26.119
Monarch is gonna want
this car in the race.


00:40:26.120 --> 00:40:30.039
Nobody knows where the race
is until you get the invite,


00:40:30.040 --> 00:40:34.239
so exactly where would
you be driving off to?


00:40:34.240 --> 00:40:36.759
Well, on the low, we
know it's in California,


00:40:36.760 --> 00:40:38.405
we just don't know where.


00:40:38.480 --> 00:40:40.479
And we also know that one
of the drivers is...


00:40:40.480 --> 00:40:42.159
- Benny.
- Okay, I'll shut up.


00:40:42.160 --> 00:40:44.959
California is quite a big state


00:40:44.960 --> 00:40:49.319
and you might remember
that I'm a numbers girl.


00:40:49.320 --> 00:40:52.279
Okay, so what are your
numbers telling you?


00:40:52.280 --> 00:40:54.679
There's a drivers' meeting
the night before the race.


00:40:54.680 --> 00:40:58.479
And that means you
have 45 hours or less


00:40:58.480 --> 00:41:03.322
to get from New York to
somewhere in California.


00:41:03.880 --> 00:41:05.650
And your problem is...


00:41:06.560 --> 00:41:08.839
We better get going.


00:41:08.840 --> 00:41:10.599
It's 45 hours and counting.


00:41:10.600 --> 00:41:12.609
Whoa, whoa, whoa! Hey, wait, wait!


00:41:13.040 --> 00:41:14.571
You're not going anywhere.


00:41:16.640 --> 00:41:18.046
You need a right-seater.


00:41:18.760 --> 00:41:22.759
And Ingram is not going
to leave this car


00:41:22.760 --> 00:41:25.611
in the hands of an ex-con


00:41:25.840 --> 00:41:29.044
who is about to leave the
state and break parole.


00:41:30.480 --> 00:41:34.810
44 hours and 59 minutes left.


00:41:35.360 --> 00:41:37.403
Let's go.


00:41:46.920 --> 00:41:48.519
Okay.


00:41:48.520 --> 00:41:51.319
Maybe we can just ditch her at
a gas station or something.


00:41:51.320 --> 00:41:52.999
Hey, man. Look, you want her gone?


00:41:53.000 --> 00:41:55.039
I'll broom her ass out. Okay?


00:41:55.040 --> 00:41:57.599
Just follow me, dude. I'll have you
driving like a bat out of hell.


00:41:57.600 --> 00:42:00.371
She'll be screaming to
get out of this car.


00:42:01.200 --> 00:42:03.368
She's just crazy, you know?


00:42:04.120 --> 00:42:05.765
She talks too much.


00:42:24.560 --> 00:42:29.119
Okay, so you've never
been a right-seater.


00:42:29.120 --> 00:42:31.399
Well, if you see something
I'm doing wrong,


00:42:31.400 --> 00:42:32.965
just point it out.


00:42:33.720 --> 00:42:36.287
First of all, you're
wearing high heels.


00:42:36.680 --> 00:42:38.962
We just call them heels.


00:42:40.600 --> 00:42:43.559
But if it's a real problem,
then I can always...


00:42:43.560 --> 00:42:45.601
I've got a change of shoes
in my overnight bag.


00:42:48.440 --> 00:42:50.005
Yep, okay.


00:42:52.920 --> 00:42:54.399
So, is there anything else


00:42:54.400 --> 00:42:57.683
that right-seaters
are supposed to do?


00:42:58.240 --> 00:42:59.805
Be quiet.


00:42:59.880 --> 00:43:02.526
Hello, Beauty. This
is Maverick speaking,


00:43:03.320 --> 00:43:05.639
the most awesome pilot
in the universe.


00:43:05.640 --> 00:43:07.119
Just wanted to give you a heads-up


00:43:07.120 --> 00:43:08.839
and tell you about a little
stop-and-go traffic up ahead.


00:43:08.840 --> 00:43:10.280
Nothing too serious.


00:43:10.520 --> 00:43:13.166
We got traffic up ahead.
We're gonna need to reroute.


00:43:16.840 --> 00:43:18.326
I don't see any traffic.


00:43:18.720 --> 00:43:22.003
Well, Benny does,
and he sees everything.


00:43:23.640 --> 00:43:25.279
All right. Now, give me a
dollar on the next exit.


00:43:25.280 --> 00:43:27.130
What's a dollar?


00:43:39.520 --> 00:43:41.563
Hard right for lane three.


00:43:42.960 --> 00:43:44.239
In three,


00:43:44.240 --> 00:43:45.359
two,


00:43:45.360 --> 00:43:46.599
- one.
- Uh, no.


00:43:46.600 --> 00:43:47.847
Now.


00:43:52.240 --> 00:43:54.239
You're looking a little
filthy down there, Beauty.


00:43:54.240 --> 00:43:55.639
- It's time to get you clean.
- What?


00:43:55.640 --> 00:43:58.650
Hard left U in three, two, one.


00:44:04.240 --> 00:44:06.681
Oh, my God!


00:44:13.680 --> 00:44:14.759
Go three...


00:44:14.760 --> 00:44:15.961
Now.


00:44:24.400 --> 00:44:25.806
You are moving, baby!


00:44:37.000 --> 00:44:40.044
You do at least see the SUV
that we are about to slam into?


00:44:45.400 --> 00:44:48.001
You meant that one? The green one?


00:44:54.280 --> 00:44:55.641
Tobey!


00:44:59.520 --> 00:45:01.404
- You see the bus, right?
- What's that?


00:45:01.520 --> 00:45:02.767
The bus!


00:45:04.560 --> 00:45:05.999
The bus! The bus! The bus!


00:45:06.000 --> 00:45:07.201
Go two, now.


00:45:11.720 --> 00:45:13.839
Looks like a scene out
of Speed down there.


00:45:13.840 --> 00:45:15.451
Hard left in three, Keanu.


00:45:17.360 --> 00:45:20.559
You mean that bus, bus, bus.


00:45:20.560 --> 00:45:23.684
Just so you know, your
friend Benny sucks.


00:45:24.680 --> 00:45:26.211
Hard left in one.


00:45:32.680 --> 00:45:34.239
My man!


00:45:34.240 --> 00:45:36.919
You got some skills, boy.
You know you bad.


00:45:36.920 --> 00:45:38.406
You know you bad!


00:45:52.160 --> 00:45:56.410
Beauty, it looks to me like you're
all clear from here, my friend.


00:45:56.560 --> 00:45:57.807
That's right.


00:45:58.160 --> 00:46:01.519
I'm just gonna keep
doing my thing, and...


00:46:01.520 --> 00:46:05.839
Fly like an eagle, to the sea


00:46:05.840 --> 00:46:09.479
Fly like an eagle
Let my spirit carry me


00:46:09.480 --> 00:46:12.604
Go on and fly!


00:46:21.160 --> 00:46:24.399
You know, I get that driving
fast is going to be necessary,


00:46:24.400 --> 00:46:27.119
but driving like a complete maniac
in order to scare me out of the car


00:46:27.120 --> 00:46:28.924
is not going to work.


00:46:29.760 --> 00:46:31.086
Are you sure about that?


00:46:33.040 --> 00:46:34.526
Is that what you think?


00:46:40.400 --> 00:46:42.728
Whatever you think about me,


00:46:43.560 --> 00:46:44.761
I'm sure it's wrong.


00:46:45.520 --> 00:46:47.848
Educate me.


00:46:48.720 --> 00:46:51.359
So you think just because


00:46:51.360 --> 00:46:53.839
I make a living buying cars
designed to triple the speed limit,


00:46:53.840 --> 00:46:56.759
and because I drive a Maserati, and
by the way, I'm an awesome driver,


00:46:56.760 --> 00:46:58.680
that you have the right
to condescend to me?


00:47:02.440 --> 00:47:08.044
Well, this is going to be the longest
44 hours and 11 minutes of your life.


00:47:15.080 --> 00:47:16.839
I'm not trying to be an asshole.


00:47:16.840 --> 00:47:19.079
You don't have to try that hard.


00:47:19.080 --> 00:47:21.519
The sound of a guy
called the Monarch


00:47:21.520 --> 00:47:23.839
who hosts a secret race
is hard to believe.


00:47:23.840 --> 00:47:25.759
He's supposedly from
an old wealthy family


00:47:25.760 --> 00:47:28.327
that made their money in
the Industrial Revolution.


00:47:28.480 --> 00:47:30.200
- And no one knows who he is?
- No one.


00:47:31.040 --> 00:47:34.919
Legend is he sponsored a
few Formula One teams


00:47:34.920 --> 00:47:36.929
but always campaigned
under other names.


00:47:37.120 --> 00:47:38.879
A man of mystery.


00:47:38.880 --> 00:47:41.048
Mystery and a bad heart.


00:47:41.080 --> 00:47:42.919
He had a dalliance as a driver,


00:47:42.920 --> 00:47:45.679
but his heart stopped
like a watch one day.


00:47:45.680 --> 00:47:47.079
So he quit.


00:47:47.080 --> 00:47:49.601
So what's the prize
for this De Leon?


00:47:50.720 --> 00:47:52.119
Well,


00:47:52.120 --> 00:47:55.279
big risks come with big rewards.


00:47:55.280 --> 00:47:58.599
Maybe that's why I walked away
with $6 million worth of cars.


00:47:58.600 --> 00:48:00.959
- That sounds like a good day's work.
- Yes, it was.


00:48:00.960 --> 00:48:05.439
Look, I don't mean to push you, but
I have another interested party.


00:48:05.440 --> 00:48:08.166
I'm not 100% sure about them.
You know that feeling?


00:48:09.120 --> 00:48:11.119
I liked what I saw
at your dealership.


00:48:11.120 --> 00:48:14.479
The problem I have is, you
haven't shown a hard profit yet.


00:48:14.480 --> 00:48:17.524
But I thought you said the
dealership was in profits last year.


00:48:22.160 --> 00:48:24.169
Let me be blunt.


00:48:24.560 --> 00:48:26.999
What do I have to do to get
a real commitment from you?


00:48:27.000 --> 00:48:29.759
I'll be blunt back.
What's a real commitment?


00:48:29.760 --> 00:48:30.961
Five million.


00:48:35.840 --> 00:48:38.399
Okay, but


00:48:38.400 --> 00:48:40.602
you have to win this
secret De Leon again.


00:48:41.160 --> 00:48:43.966
And all those cars
that come with it.


00:49:02.960 --> 00:49:04.439
Yo.


00:49:04.440 --> 00:49:06.085
Checking in.


00:49:06.880 --> 00:49:10.562
Mile marker 417. We're on schedule.


00:49:11.160 --> 00:49:14.807
I know we're on schedule.
I'm checking on you, bro.


00:49:15.680 --> 00:49:18.087
I was just sitting here thinking,


00:49:19.760 --> 00:49:21.724
Pete would have loved this trip.


00:49:22.360 --> 00:49:23.800
Yeah.


00:49:25.360 --> 00:49:28.439
He loved the impossible, huh?


00:49:28.440 --> 00:49:30.961
Perfect for Petey.


00:49:32.400 --> 00:49:34.443
Where's your head at, brother?


00:49:35.040 --> 00:49:37.766
I'll never forget
what I saw that day.


00:49:38.840 --> 00:49:40.879
Listen, don't you worry.


00:49:40.880 --> 00:49:43.242
Dino's gonna get
what's coming to him.


00:49:43.560 --> 00:49:46.730
Just don't forget why
we're doing this.


00:49:48.400 --> 00:49:51.763
I'll see you in Detroit,
brother. Beast out.


00:49:59.760 --> 00:50:02.167
I'm sorry about Pete.


00:50:09.600 --> 00:50:12.280
He just left him there.


00:50:13.800 --> 00:50:17.129
That's what I can't forgive.


00:50:19.440 --> 00:50:22.803
That's what this is really
about then, isn't it?


00:50:48.840 --> 00:50:50.201
Good morning.


00:51:07.080 --> 00:51:10.799
Dude, stop calling me, okay? We've
already had this conversation.


00:51:10.800 --> 00:51:13.287
- Just go to the window.
- No.


00:51:14.840 --> 00:51:16.087
Why?


00:51:16.680 --> 00:51:19.531
Just go to the window.
Quit being a little bitch.


00:51:21.400 --> 00:51:23.125
You're the bitch.


00:51:38.000 --> 00:51:40.839
Unit 4-Adam, report of noise
complaint, Woodward circle.


00:51:40.840 --> 00:51:42.279
Vehicle description, silver Ford...


00:51:42.280 --> 00:51:44.323
What the hell are you doing?


00:51:45.000 --> 00:51:47.199
- Keeping the engine hot.
- Unit 4 responding.


00:51:47.200 --> 00:51:49.641
You're gonna attract
attention to yourself.


00:51:53.520 --> 00:51:55.882
Shit.


00:52:01.280 --> 00:52:03.403
Is that your car, son?


00:52:04.040 --> 00:52:07.119
No, no, no, no, no.


00:52:07.120 --> 00:52:10.563
Are you crazy? Do you know
how expensive this car is?


00:52:10.880 --> 00:52:13.239
Why don't you just take
it around the corner?


00:52:13.240 --> 00:52:16.759
Hey, hey, did you see
how fast I was going?


00:52:16.760 --> 00:52:20.559
It must have been, like,
160 on that off-ramp.


00:52:20.560 --> 00:52:23.399
You should drive this car.
It's amazing!


00:52:23.400 --> 00:52:26.559
- Officer, I am so sorry.
- It's insane! Insane.


00:52:26.560 --> 00:52:29.359
My boyfriend was showing off.
He's trying to impress me.


00:52:29.360 --> 00:52:32.803
Why don't we just take it
around the block? Now.


00:52:36.960 --> 00:52:38.730
"Boyfriend"?


00:52:39.280 --> 00:52:41.448
I'm just trying to
keep us out of jail.


00:52:42.040 --> 00:52:45.130
Well, you might wanna
fix your hair.


00:52:48.880 --> 00:52:50.879
For my mug shot?


00:52:50.880 --> 00:52:52.081
No.


00:52:54.080 --> 00:52:57.170
Because I'm about
to make you famous.


00:52:58.480 --> 00:52:59.759
Finn, are you there?


00:52:59.760 --> 00:53:01.599
- I'm here.
- All right.


00:53:01.600 --> 00:53:03.279
Don't mind the cop.
That's not the problem.


00:53:03.280 --> 00:53:05.439
Watch how the car leans
as he pulls away.


00:53:05.440 --> 00:53:07.449
That's our problem.


00:53:08.440 --> 00:53:09.641
Go, go!


00:53:24.080 --> 00:53:26.760
In pursuit, modified Ford Mustang.


00:53:29.640 --> 00:53:32.366
Heading east on Woodward.


00:53:35.640 --> 00:53:37.001
The car is loose.


00:53:37.120 --> 00:53:38.799
Yeah, I know. Thank you for that.


00:53:38.800 --> 00:53:42.359
If Tobey runs that setup in De Leon,
he won't finish, let alone win.


00:53:42.360 --> 00:53:43.561
He's in?


00:53:44.120 --> 00:53:45.321
Maybe.


00:53:45.640 --> 00:53:46.719
Look, we have a plan.


00:53:46.720 --> 00:53:48.199
And what does that mean?


00:53:48.200 --> 00:53:50.971
It means we know what we're doing.
Get your ass down here, bitch.


00:54:08.240 --> 00:54:10.442
Finn! Finn, you okay, buddy?


00:54:16.240 --> 00:54:18.169
Casual Friday.


00:54:19.000 --> 00:54:20.690
Finn, man, what's up?


00:54:24.760 --> 00:54:27.964
Jacki.


00:54:33.760 --> 00:54:36.167
I've always wanted to do that.


00:54:36.640 --> 00:54:38.251
Yeah!


00:54:42.880 --> 00:54:46.050
Have a nice day, you
miserable bastards.


00:54:51.640 --> 00:54:53.490
Finn, call me!


00:55:02.200 --> 00:55:04.679
My friend is running the
fastest Mustang in the world


00:55:04.680 --> 00:55:05.879
at De Leon on Sunday


00:55:05.880 --> 00:55:08.162
and the setup is all wrong.


00:55:09.240 --> 00:55:11.886
I'm in accounting.


00:55:12.720 --> 00:55:15.319
Don't you feel like
you're dying inside?


00:55:15.320 --> 00:55:16.726
Yes.


00:55:20.000 --> 00:55:22.089
It's cold in here.


00:55:31.120 --> 00:55:32.890
Where's the Beast?


00:55:33.200 --> 00:55:34.719
What the hell?


00:55:34.720 --> 00:55:36.079
- Where are your clothes?
- Did you miss this?


00:55:36.080 --> 00:55:38.079
No, I didn't miss it.
Don't touch me, man.


00:55:38.080 --> 00:55:39.879
Stay away! We gotta go, let's go.


00:55:39.880 --> 00:55:41.119
You missed me, didn't you?


00:55:41.120 --> 00:55:42.845
No. Get off!


00:55:43.720 --> 00:55:46.119
I've got the shaved bird.
We're jumping in the Beast.


00:55:46.120 --> 00:55:48.919
We're behind. We got 28
hours to get to Cali.


00:55:48.920 --> 00:55:50.079
Copy that.


00:55:50.080 --> 00:55:51.799
- Good morning.
- Oh, my God.


00:55:51.800 --> 00:55:53.679
So, why the hell are you naked?


00:55:53.680 --> 00:55:55.279
To make sure I'd never come back.


00:55:55.280 --> 00:55:56.679
I'm sure you could've
done that another way.


00:55:56.680 --> 00:55:59.690
Let's be clear, though, you're
not wearing my underwear.


00:56:07.120 --> 00:56:10.164
There's a helicopter in
the middle of the street.


00:56:15.800 --> 00:56:16.959
Hello?


00:56:16.960 --> 00:56:20.119
WNKW with a question
for Tobey Marshall.


00:56:20.120 --> 00:56:23.767
On a scale from one to ten,
how crazy hot is your passenger?


00:56:25.080 --> 00:56:28.045
Like my new wheels?
Bitchin', right?


00:56:30.080 --> 00:56:31.799
What happened to the Cessna?


00:56:31.800 --> 00:56:33.679
Flight restrictions
in the city, man.


00:56:33.680 --> 00:56:35.919
But it's all good. I borrowed
my buddy's little bird.


00:56:35.920 --> 00:56:37.201
Let me get a hard right.


00:56:48.320 --> 00:56:50.399
Y'all lucky, I almost got
my hands on that Apache


00:56:50.400 --> 00:56:51.959
from Great Lakes Army Air Base,


00:56:51.960 --> 00:56:54.561
but Colonel Gatins was
sweating me hard.


00:56:54.680 --> 00:56:55.961
Here we go again.


00:56:56.000 --> 00:56:57.645
Not talking to you, Beast.


00:57:02.640 --> 00:57:04.639
Roger that, Liar One.


00:57:04.640 --> 00:57:06.239
Finn, you're back in the
crew for all of 10 minutes


00:57:06.240 --> 00:57:08.519
and you're already up
my skirt talking shit.


00:57:08.520 --> 00:57:11.001
Man, you're gonna rue the day
you started calling me that.


00:57:13.800 --> 00:57:16.279
What, did you all of a
sudden go to college, fool?


00:57:16.280 --> 00:57:18.479
Wow. What a really
ignorant thing to say.


00:57:18.480 --> 00:57:20.919
God, are you ignorant.


00:57:20.920 --> 00:57:22.963
Is it gonna be like
this the entire way?


00:57:27.960 --> 00:57:31.801
A reminder, the Motown Marathon
races through town this weekend...


00:57:32.120 --> 00:57:33.959
Romeo, stand by.


00:57:33.960 --> 00:57:36.919
Standing by.


00:57:36.920 --> 00:57:39.719
But for today's traffic,
we go live to Romeo


00:57:39.720 --> 00:57:41.559
in the Channel 10
traffic helicopter.


00:57:41.560 --> 00:57:43.683
- How are we looking, Romeo?
- Cut to two.


00:57:44.200 --> 00:57:45.919
Bum


00:57:45.920 --> 00:57:48.399
Bum, bum, bum, bum!


00:57:48.400 --> 00:57:50.479
Is Romeo in the helicopter?
What's going on?


00:57:50.480 --> 00:57:52.199
Bum, bum


00:57:52.200 --> 00:57:53.925
Looking good, Beth.


00:57:54.120 --> 00:57:56.004
Real good.


00:57:56.800 --> 00:57:59.399
Commercial! Hey, cut to commercial!


00:57:59.400 --> 00:58:01.648
Hey, Liar One, eyes on the road.


00:58:01.680 --> 00:58:03.689
Wow!


00:58:04.080 --> 00:58:05.486
I did not see that.


00:58:08.720 --> 00:58:11.199
5-Charlie, I got ops
on the silver Mustang.


00:58:11.200 --> 00:58:13.599
I'm in pursuit.
Westbound Jefferson.


00:58:13.600 --> 00:58:15.079
Copy, 7-Charlie.


00:58:15.080 --> 00:58:17.601
We'll stop him before
he gets on the 375.


00:58:39.440 --> 00:58:41.639
All right, Beauty, this
is gonna sound insane,


00:58:41.640 --> 00:58:44.639
but I need a two-lane grasshopper in
order to get these guys off your back.


00:58:44.640 --> 00:58:46.319
- Roger.
- What's a grasshopper?


00:58:46.320 --> 00:58:48.568
You may wanna close
your eyes for this.


00:58:49.120 --> 00:58:50.651
Is it worse than "Bus, bus, bus"?


00:58:55.520 --> 00:58:57.688
All right. Now, just
aim for the trees.


00:59:00.120 --> 00:59:01.446
Spread your wings, Beauty!


00:59:32.040 --> 00:59:34.599
What just happened? You're amazing.


00:59:34.600 --> 00:59:36.279
I can't believe we're alive.


00:59:36.280 --> 00:59:39.051
Okay, got to go.
Time's up in the bird.


00:59:39.280 --> 00:59:42.399
That was amazing. You're amazing.


00:59:42.400 --> 00:59:43.959
We are amazing.


00:59:43.960 --> 00:59:47.719
All units, please be advised,
silver Mustang last seen on 375.


00:59:47.720 --> 00:59:50.082
Need to contact State
for air support.


00:59:50.840 --> 00:59:52.639
State dispatch status on Arrow One.


00:59:52.640 --> 00:59:54.439
Needed for immediate
officer assistance.


00:59:54.440 --> 00:59:57.405
Suspect believed to be
heading westbound on 94.


00:59:57.560 --> 01:00:00.525
Arrow One en route. ETA is in five.


01:00:24.320 --> 01:00:27.410
Liar One, are you tracking
that air bear heading to I-94?


01:00:27.640 --> 01:00:31.039
If he spots me, it's game over.
We're gonna need to switch to plan B.


01:00:31.040 --> 01:00:32.799
Plan B adds an hour to the trip.


01:00:32.800 --> 01:00:34.959
No choice, we're gonna
have to make up that time.


01:00:34.960 --> 01:00:36.119
Roger that. Plan B it is.


01:00:36.120 --> 01:00:37.919
Beauty will go bingo on that route,


01:00:37.920 --> 01:00:40.399
so we're gonna have to
hot fuel and top off.


01:00:40.400 --> 01:00:42.648
Hot fuel, coming up!


01:00:43.200 --> 01:00:44.447
Get out there, skinny boy.


01:00:44.840 --> 01:00:47.122
You were checking me out!


01:00:53.320 --> 01:00:54.521
What?


01:00:54.880 --> 01:00:57.481
"Bingo" and "hot fuel"...


01:00:57.960 --> 01:01:00.559
We're refueling without stopping.


01:01:00.560 --> 01:01:02.285
So why don't you just say that?


01:01:04.440 --> 01:01:07.610
Well, I mean, I guess
I could, but...


01:01:36.960 --> 01:01:38.321
What are you doing?


01:01:39.160 --> 01:01:40.361
Helping.


01:01:40.840 --> 01:01:42.121
What?


01:01:44.000 --> 01:01:45.326
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!


01:01:47.000 --> 01:01:48.247
Shit!


01:01:48.920 --> 01:01:50.360
Steady!


01:01:58.840 --> 01:02:00.451
Closer!


01:02:08.960 --> 01:02:10.446
- Yeah!
- All right!


01:02:16.400 --> 01:02:17.761
I got this!


01:02:18.680 --> 01:02:19.881
Go inside!


01:02:23.160 --> 01:02:25.567
The hits just keep on
coming with you, huh?


01:02:25.960 --> 01:02:28.242
Never judge a girl
by her Gucci boots.


01:02:28.360 --> 01:02:29.561
Her what?


01:02:30.760 --> 01:02:32.371
High heels.


01:02:33.200 --> 01:02:34.526
Why don't you just say that?


01:02:36.520 --> 01:02:37.721
Nice.


01:02:37.840 --> 01:02:39.963
Hey, Beast, take the
shoulder, I'll go with you.


01:02:40.280 --> 01:02:41.720
Roger that, Beauty.


01:02:42.440 --> 01:02:43.639
All units be advised,


01:02:43.640 --> 01:02:45.359
we're on the lookout
for a silver Mustang,


01:02:45.360 --> 01:02:49.439
Adam-David-Tom 4-6-1-9,
heading westbound on 94.


01:02:49.440 --> 01:02:50.799
Arrow One, 10-4?


01:02:50.800 --> 01:02:53.359
I need eyes on that bear
in the air, Liar One.


01:02:53.360 --> 01:02:54.561
What's your 20?


01:02:54.720 --> 01:02:56.251
Still on the ground, Beauty.


01:02:58.480 --> 01:03:00.879
Come on, Susan.


01:03:00.880 --> 01:03:04.687
Don't let me down, baby. Come on...


01:03:10.120 --> 01:03:11.890
Yeah!


01:03:12.280 --> 01:03:13.481
That's my girl.


01:03:15.960 --> 01:03:17.844
Arrow. ETA in one.


01:03:28.360 --> 01:03:29.479
You're good!


01:03:29.480 --> 01:03:30.681
We're clear.


01:03:31.760 --> 01:03:33.200
Yeah, yeah!


01:03:39.080 --> 01:03:40.399
Thanks, boys!


01:03:40.400 --> 01:03:42.039
Beauty is a redneck.


01:03:42.040 --> 01:03:44.641
Roger that. Beast loves a redneck.


01:03:55.560 --> 01:03:58.119
Yeah!


01:03:58.120 --> 01:04:00.891
Dispatch, this is Arrow One.
10-97 in the area.


01:04:02.400 --> 01:04:04.364
No visual at this time.


01:04:05.320 --> 01:04:08.126
Bear in the air is
fangs-out down I-94.


01:04:08.400 --> 01:04:11.410
Beauty, you are safe and sound.


01:04:13.880 --> 01:04:16.526
"Redneck"? So, we're heading south.


01:04:34.720 --> 01:04:35.959
All units be advised,


01:04:35.960 --> 01:04:39.679
Ford Mustang, New York plate
Adam-David-Tom 4-6-1-9,


01:04:39.680 --> 01:04:41.999
last seen headed westbound on 94.


01:04:42.000 --> 01:04:43.599
Possible named suspect.


01:04:43.600 --> 01:04:47.399
Tobey Marshall, wanted
on parole violation and GTA.


01:04:47.400 --> 01:04:49.959
Passenger described as a
blonde, white female,


01:04:49.960 --> 01:04:51.525
identity still unknown.


01:04:54.960 --> 01:04:56.685
It was just a matter of time.


01:04:57.760 --> 01:05:01.079
Yeah, well, you sped it up with
your little stunt in Detroit.


01:05:01.080 --> 01:05:03.408
It had to be done.


01:05:03.960 --> 01:05:05.685
To get Finn?


01:05:06.560 --> 01:05:07.761
No, not just that.


01:05:10.160 --> 01:05:13.682
Kids, I'm looking at something
that I can't quite believe.


01:05:13.840 --> 01:05:16.599
I mean, my inbox is white hot.


01:05:16.600 --> 01:05:18.679
I got a bunch of trolls
sending me footage


01:05:18.680 --> 01:05:21.326
of something that is mind-blowing.


01:05:21.920 --> 01:05:27.126
I'm looking at footage of a car
that supposedly disappeared.


01:05:29.000 --> 01:05:33.999
That's the same car that Ford
and Shelby were building


01:05:34.000 --> 01:05:35.531
when Carroll died.


01:05:36.360 --> 01:05:39.131
I'm looking at a gorgeous ghost.


01:05:44.040 --> 01:05:48.319
And I think that's Tobey
Marshall inside there,


01:05:48.320 --> 01:05:51.679
driving a chariot of the gods.


01:05:51.680 --> 01:05:54.804
So I bow down to Tobey Marshall.


01:05:55.680 --> 01:05:58.479
Dino Brewster is on the
line right now. Dino!


01:05:58.480 --> 01:06:01.411
Dino, Dino bambino
in San Francisco.


01:06:01.560 --> 01:06:03.559
You need to see
what I'm looking at.


01:06:03.560 --> 01:06:06.159
I'm looking at some aerial
footage of Tobey Marshall


01:06:06.160 --> 01:06:08.761
flying across the country
with the cops in tow,


01:06:08.800 --> 01:06:11.890
in a phantom Ford that will
make your bowels loose.


01:06:12.320 --> 01:06:16.239
Tobey Marshall doing something
stupid and reckless again?


01:06:16.240 --> 01:06:19.799
Didn't that guy just get out
of prison for manslaughter?


01:06:19.800 --> 01:06:23.399
Whoa! Dino, Dino, bambino.
Hey, accidents happen in racing.


01:06:23.400 --> 01:06:26.410
Nobody knows that better
than you, Dino, remember?


01:06:27.720 --> 01:06:30.919
I just don't wanna see
him race at De Leon.


01:06:30.920 --> 01:06:32.719
You know, in fact,


01:06:32.720 --> 01:06:35.764
I'm willing to give up my...


01:06:36.040 --> 01:06:37.999
I'm willing to give up my Elemento


01:06:38.000 --> 01:06:40.806
to anyone that puts a
stop to Tobey Marshall.


01:06:42.760 --> 01:06:43.999
Wait a minute.


01:06:44.000 --> 01:06:46.159
Wait a minute, did you just
say what I think you said?


01:06:46.160 --> 01:06:48.759
That car is one of
three in the world.


01:06:48.760 --> 01:06:51.439
You're willing to give
away your Lamborghini


01:06:51.440 --> 01:06:52.559
to stop Tobey Marshall?


01:06:52.560 --> 01:06:56.685
Yes, I am. And I'm gonna
post some pictures online


01:06:57.440 --> 01:07:01.770
so everybody knows exactly
what they're looking for.


01:07:03.840 --> 01:07:07.279
This is too good.


01:07:07.280 --> 01:07:11.239
I got star-crossed lovers
hauling ass across the country.


01:07:11.240 --> 01:07:15.240
I got Dino Brewster, who just painted
a huge bull's-eye on their ass.


01:07:16.200 --> 01:07:19.439
Man. Christmas came
early, wing nuts.


01:07:19.440 --> 01:07:23.770
The thing you gotta understand
is, racing is an art.


01:07:24.640 --> 01:07:27.759
Douchebag is out here,
he wants to talk to you.


01:07:27.760 --> 01:07:29.639
Racing with passion...


01:07:29.640 --> 01:07:32.571
Dude, that's high art.


01:07:35.480 --> 01:07:38.081
Man, I can feel love and vengeance


01:07:39.040 --> 01:07:42.159
and smell motor oil all
swirling together out there.


01:07:42.160 --> 01:07:44.799
We got supernatural Mustangs,
we got personal vendettas.


01:07:44.800 --> 01:07:48.482
I have no idea where this is going.
I just know I like it. I like it a lot!


01:07:49.080 --> 01:07:50.999
Call in, defend yourself.


01:07:51.000 --> 01:07:53.362
Everyone knows my story.


01:07:55.160 --> 01:07:56.361
Go ahead.


01:07:56.640 --> 01:08:01.209
Monarch, this is the blonde female
sitting right next to Tobey Marshall.


01:08:01.840 --> 01:08:03.319
Really? Okay.


01:08:03.320 --> 01:08:05.999
We got a girl with a
fake British accent,


01:08:06.000 --> 01:08:07.839
claiming she's sitting
next to Tobey Marshall.


01:08:07.840 --> 01:08:10.042
Having a spot of
tea, are you, dove?


01:08:19.040 --> 01:08:22.599
There were three cars in the race the
day that Pete died, that's a fact.


01:08:22.600 --> 01:08:24.519
And anyone that says that
Tobey is responsible


01:08:24.520 --> 01:08:26.679
for Pete's death, answer this.


01:08:26.680 --> 01:08:28.679
Why jump parole in New York


01:08:28.680 --> 01:08:31.719
knowing that you are going to be
re-arrested and do serious time,


01:08:31.720 --> 01:08:34.969
unless you are innocent and
hell-bent to right a wrong?


01:08:36.480 --> 01:08:40.924
He did the time, he paid the
debts, why would he risk it?


01:08:42.360 --> 01:08:45.928
Next time you talk to Dino,
you can ask him that question.


01:08:53.600 --> 01:08:55.211
Thank you.


01:08:56.840 --> 01:08:58.769
You're welcome.


01:09:02.280 --> 01:09:04.839
I like this girl.


01:09:04.840 --> 01:09:07.119
Yeah! Yeah!


01:09:07.120 --> 01:09:11.039
Yeah, the British are coming.
I gotta tell you, I'm moved. I am.


01:09:11.040 --> 01:09:14.679
The whole thing just went
right here to the old ticker.


01:09:14.680 --> 01:09:17.239
I gotta pop one of these.


01:09:17.240 --> 01:09:18.441
Yeah.


01:09:18.880 --> 01:09:20.605
This is getting good.


01:09:21.680 --> 01:09:23.723
I believe you, you
crazy little tart.


01:09:24.520 --> 01:09:27.079
Tobey Marshall versus
Dino Brewster.


01:09:27.080 --> 01:09:30.079
That's a deep rivalry right there.


01:09:30.080 --> 01:09:34.649
Yeah. I hear you,
honey. I hear you.


01:09:35.720 --> 01:09:37.279
The two of you out there,


01:09:37.280 --> 01:09:39.959
flying across the country at
killer speeds to prove something


01:09:39.960 --> 01:09:42.479
while you're tearing up
the American asphalt.


01:09:42.480 --> 01:09:45.968
Born to run, baby. Born to run.


01:09:46.560 --> 01:09:47.966
Tobey Marshall,


01:09:48.560 --> 01:09:50.683
welcome to the De Leon.


01:09:59.920 --> 01:10:02.279
That's it, cretins,


01:10:02.280 --> 01:10:04.482
De Leon is full.


01:10:04.960 --> 01:10:07.159
But if you want Dino
Brewster's Lamborghini,


01:10:07.160 --> 01:10:10.409
you're gonna have to chase
down that Mustang to get it.


01:10:10.760 --> 01:10:11.961
Wow.


01:10:13.280 --> 01:10:15.479
The race before the race.


01:10:15.480 --> 01:10:17.364
I love it.


01:11:25.960 --> 01:11:27.359
Beauty!


01:11:27.360 --> 01:11:30.245
Congrats on the wild card
to the rodeo, my friend.


01:11:30.360 --> 01:11:33.119
Your route is clear to
the Nebraska border.


01:11:33.120 --> 01:11:34.359
Darkness is upon us,


01:11:34.360 --> 01:11:36.439
so the eyes in the sky
will be shut for a while.


01:11:36.440 --> 01:11:38.802
But I'm gonna leapfrog ahead and
meet you guys at Record Breaker.


01:11:38.840 --> 01:11:40.451
What's your 20, Liar One?


01:11:40.720 --> 01:11:43.082
Flat-hatting you, bitch!


01:11:47.960 --> 01:11:49.279
Special delivery.


01:11:49.280 --> 01:11:51.599
I hope you ladies didn't soil
your panties down there.


01:11:51.600 --> 01:11:52.799
I hate it when he does that!


01:11:52.800 --> 01:11:55.639
That's what I thought.
Keep talking that shit.


01:11:55.640 --> 01:11:58.079
Nice to see you haven't
changed, nimrod.


01:11:58.080 --> 01:11:59.879
Okay, listen. I don't
know who "nimrod" is,


01:11:59.880 --> 01:12:01.919
but I'm pretty sure
he lived in the '50s.


01:12:01.920 --> 01:12:05.249
All right? My handle is Maverick.


01:12:05.400 --> 01:12:07.443
You better ask somebody.


01:12:23.480 --> 01:12:25.439
Hey, make it fast, we're
two hours behind schedule.


01:12:25.440 --> 01:12:26.641
Okay, I got this.


01:13:16.480 --> 01:13:17.679
Large coffee, please.


01:13:17.680 --> 01:13:19.280
- Cream and sugar?
- No, just black.


01:13:45.680 --> 01:13:48.804
Yeah. I can't talk. I know.


01:13:48.880 --> 01:13:51.731
Excuse me, miss. Can I
ask you a few questions?


01:13:52.160 --> 01:13:53.999
Why, of course you can,


01:13:54.000 --> 01:13:56.239
Officer Lejeune.


01:13:56.240 --> 01:13:58.408
How can I help you?


01:13:59.600 --> 01:14:01.239
Do you live in the area?


01:14:01.240 --> 01:14:04.639
No, sir. We're actually
just long hauling.


01:14:04.640 --> 01:14:06.799
Where from?


01:14:06.800 --> 01:14:08.839
From south to north.


01:14:08.840 --> 01:14:11.771
So we actually started
in Louisiana.


01:14:12.840 --> 01:14:15.646
So you are not traveling in
that silver Mustang out front?


01:14:16.760 --> 01:14:18.519
Mustang?


01:14:18.520 --> 01:14:21.479
What, like the horse?


01:14:21.480 --> 01:14:22.841
No, sir. No.


01:14:24.600 --> 01:14:27.199
I'd like to ask you a
few more questions.


01:14:27.200 --> 01:14:30.370
If you'd step out to my cruiser,
shouldn't take but a minute.


01:14:35.480 --> 01:14:36.681
Stop!


01:14:42.280 --> 01:14:43.686
Stop right there!


01:14:52.520 --> 01:14:54.039
Tobey? He's following me.


01:14:54.040 --> 01:14:55.879
I know. Where are you?


01:14:55.880 --> 01:14:57.359
I'm upstairs. I'm in a room.


01:14:57.360 --> 01:14:59.289
All right, is there a window?


01:15:00.720 --> 01:15:02.570
It's on the second floor.


01:15:02.960 --> 01:15:04.559
Open up this door!


01:15:04.560 --> 01:15:07.079
Look, just climb out the window.
I'll come get you.


01:15:07.080 --> 01:15:08.239
Okay.


01:15:08.240 --> 01:15:11.284
I'm gonna tell you one more
time, open up this door!


01:15:16.280 --> 01:15:17.845
Any units in the area? Over.


01:15:19.080 --> 01:15:21.123
Ma'am, other units
are on their way.


01:15:26.120 --> 01:15:27.321
Where are you?


01:15:37.000 --> 01:15:38.559
Hey, you gotta jump. Let's go,


01:15:38.560 --> 01:15:40.489
No, I can't jump.
I'm afraid of heights.


01:15:42.800 --> 01:15:44.239
It's not high. Come on.


01:15:44.240 --> 01:15:45.839
No, I can't. I'm afraid of heights.


01:15:45.840 --> 01:15:47.999
- I don't know what to do!
- Just trust me. Sit down.


01:15:48.000 --> 01:15:49.326
Okay? Sit down.


01:15:51.640 --> 01:15:53.879
Just close your eyes
and count to three.


01:15:53.880 --> 01:15:55.439
All right? On three.


01:15:55.440 --> 01:15:56.926
One, two...


01:16:02.880 --> 01:16:06.926
Unit 445, there are no other
units available at this time.


01:16:09.480 --> 01:16:11.808
Copy that. In pursuit
of the silver Mustang.


01:16:36.160 --> 01:16:37.361
Where is he?


01:16:37.520 --> 01:16:39.051
He's not coming.


01:16:40.080 --> 01:16:41.486
Are you sure?


01:16:42.120 --> 01:16:44.163
Trust me.


01:16:47.000 --> 01:16:49.089
Hey, you know...


01:16:49.680 --> 01:16:53.362
That was really
impressive back there.


01:16:53.840 --> 01:16:56.407
I just thought you should know.


01:17:01.840 --> 01:17:06.250
Hey, do you think you could
drive for a few hours?


01:17:10.560 --> 01:17:12.888
Let's just... Let's switch.


01:17:14.520 --> 01:17:16.210
It's all right.


01:17:17.720 --> 01:17:19.559
Okay, steady.


01:17:19.560 --> 01:17:21.842
There you go.


01:17:22.920 --> 01:17:25.168
All right, don't kill us.


01:17:36.480 --> 01:17:37.841
That's nice.


01:17:38.600 --> 01:17:39.999
Have you got her?


01:17:40.000 --> 01:17:41.770
- Yeah.
- All right.


01:17:43.560 --> 01:17:45.046
Good.


01:17:45.320 --> 01:17:47.841
Good, good, good.


01:18:42.720 --> 01:18:44.319
Jesus!


01:18:44.320 --> 01:18:45.359
That was on purpose.


01:18:45.360 --> 01:18:46.925
Yeah, thanks to Dino's bounty.


01:18:49.640 --> 01:18:51.001
They're coming at you.


01:18:52.640 --> 01:18:54.001
Copy that.


01:18:55.120 --> 01:18:57.079
Wait, wait. See? They're
trying to trap us.


01:18:57.080 --> 01:18:58.399
Here, just drift onto the shoulder.


01:18:58.400 --> 01:19:00.039
No, no, no, I'm going
for the Hummer.


01:19:00.040 --> 01:19:01.479
He's a pavement prowler.


01:19:01.480 --> 01:19:02.599
Pavement what?


01:19:02.600 --> 01:19:05.039
It's a show car with
a big lift kit.


01:19:05.040 --> 01:19:07.686
It makes up for his
inferiority complex.


01:19:12.840 --> 01:19:14.041
Wait. Are you crazy?


01:19:16.080 --> 01:19:17.930
Wait, wait! Whoa, whoa!


01:19:21.520 --> 01:19:23.210
Whoa! Jesus!


01:19:27.120 --> 01:19:28.810
You are crazy!


01:19:30.440 --> 01:19:32.483
Nice. Nice, nice.


01:19:42.440 --> 01:19:43.721
No, keep it straight!


01:19:48.040 --> 01:19:49.241
Holy shit.


01:19:50.120 --> 01:19:51.560
Okay, Larry, bring it.


01:19:51.640 --> 01:19:53.922
Got it. We're moving out.


01:19:56.640 --> 01:19:58.683
Shoot the tires, but
don't kill them.


01:20:03.680 --> 01:20:04.919
All right. Now, when I say,


01:20:04.920 --> 01:20:07.439
you're gonna let up on the gas and
you're gonna make a hard left.


01:20:07.440 --> 01:20:08.519
- Okay?
- Okay.


01:20:08.520 --> 01:20:09.559
- Okay!
- Okay.


01:20:09.560 --> 01:20:10.999
Your instincts are gonna say...


01:20:11.000 --> 01:20:12.201
Just do it!


01:20:13.520 --> 01:20:14.767
Now!


01:20:23.800 --> 01:20:25.047
Don't let up.


01:20:27.200 --> 01:20:29.320
Blast those buggers.
We'll get them on the split.


01:20:42.920 --> 01:20:44.884
Hey, Liar One, you
got your ears on?


01:20:50.480 --> 01:20:51.727
Son of a bitch!


01:20:53.360 --> 01:20:54.721
We need to find another road.


01:20:57.000 --> 01:20:58.725
Liar One, we need you!


01:21:06.560 --> 01:21:08.171
You gotta go faster.


01:21:10.480 --> 01:21:12.170
No, two hands on the wheel!


01:21:21.960 --> 01:21:23.321
Shit!


01:21:34.200 --> 01:21:35.765
Liar One, is that you?


01:21:40.160 --> 01:21:41.521
Hook up, hook up!


01:21:47.160 --> 01:21:49.681
Sergeant Jackson, this is
not what we discussed.


01:21:49.840 --> 01:21:52.239
Sir, will you relax? Okay?


01:21:52.240 --> 01:21:53.851
I got this.


01:22:00.800 --> 01:22:01.959
We're good!


01:22:01.960 --> 01:22:04.811
You gotta tell me you believe I can
fly an Apache helicopter, man.


01:22:05.240 --> 01:22:07.204
- What?
- I'm serious, bro.


01:22:07.640 --> 01:22:09.479
You're always trying to play me.


01:22:09.480 --> 01:22:11.199
Tell me you believe I can
fly an Apache helicopter.


01:22:11.200 --> 01:22:13.039
Tell him whatever he wants!


01:22:13.040 --> 01:22:15.049
Yeah, you can fly an
Apache helicopter!


01:22:15.360 --> 01:22:16.519
And my handle is Maverick.


01:22:16.520 --> 01:22:18.281
Gotta call me Maverick,
let me hear it.


01:22:18.360 --> 01:22:20.210
Maverick! Maverick!


01:22:20.320 --> 01:22:21.726
Maverick!


01:22:22.160 --> 01:22:23.885
Was that so bad?


01:22:24.040 --> 01:22:25.199
Shit!


01:22:25.200 --> 01:22:26.526
Benny!


01:22:31.200 --> 01:22:32.970
Holy shit!


01:22:47.320 --> 01:22:50.171
- Oh, my God! Oh, my God!
- Julia, hey!


01:22:50.200 --> 01:22:51.606
Look at me.


01:22:52.760 --> 01:22:54.530
Just breathe. Breathe.


01:22:56.560 --> 01:22:58.489
Good.


01:23:03.160 --> 01:23:04.999
Look into my eyes.


01:23:05.000 --> 01:23:07.248
Look into my eyes. Good.


01:23:08.520 --> 01:23:10.449
What color are they?


01:23:12.120 --> 01:23:14.402
They're really blue.


01:23:14.440 --> 01:23:16.519
They're really blue. Good, good.


01:23:16.520 --> 01:23:19.319
They're a lot bluer than yours.


01:23:19.320 --> 01:23:21.079
- No!
- Yes, they are.


01:23:21.080 --> 01:23:22.799
- They're not!
- Yes!


01:23:22.800 --> 01:23:24.199
They're not bluer!


01:23:24.200 --> 01:23:26.607
- Admit it!
- Mine are bluer!


01:23:28.240 --> 01:23:29.851
- Oh, God!
- Wow.


01:23:31.720 --> 01:23:33.959
Benny! Don't drop us!


01:23:33.960 --> 01:23:35.161
What?


01:23:35.880 --> 01:23:37.599
I'm kidding. I'm kidding.


01:23:37.600 --> 01:23:39.529
I'm kidding. We're
good, we're good.


01:23:50.800 --> 01:23:52.001
What the hell is that?


01:24:07.080 --> 01:24:08.406
Yeah!


01:24:09.320 --> 01:24:10.999
Yeah!


01:24:11.000 --> 01:24:13.079
Yeah, Tobey!


01:24:13.080 --> 01:24:14.566
Hey, Benny!


01:24:14.640 --> 01:24:16.399
We believe you, baby!


01:24:16.400 --> 01:24:18.648
We believe you, Maverick!


01:24:22.640 --> 01:24:24.679
Look at me, bitches!


01:24:24.680 --> 01:24:26.086
We're good!


01:24:26.520 --> 01:24:27.721
Yeah!


01:24:29.640 --> 01:24:30.966
Go!


01:24:39.360 --> 01:24:40.719
Are you guys Okay?


01:24:40.720 --> 01:24:41.921
Yeah.


01:24:47.960 --> 01:24:51.639
Major Davis, you are in
violation of your flight plan.


01:24:51.640 --> 01:24:52.841
My bad.


01:24:52.960 --> 01:24:55.686
Return that bird to
base immediately.


01:24:57.200 --> 01:24:59.359
Looks like I'm gonna have to
go away for a while, y'all.


01:24:59.360 --> 01:25:01.562
But Benny always comes back.


01:25:03.360 --> 01:25:07.167
Godspeed, boys. Godspeed.


01:26:07.160 --> 01:26:09.647
You're 23 minutes late.


01:26:16.720 --> 01:26:18.843
- Are you checking in, sir?
- I'll be right back.


01:26:38.600 --> 01:26:41.167
I'm surprised you made it.


01:26:41.600 --> 01:26:43.689
I'm impressed.


01:26:45.480 --> 01:26:48.365
What's going on in that
head of yours, Tobey?


01:26:49.680 --> 01:26:52.326
You never went back for him.


01:26:53.720 --> 01:26:55.763
I wasn't there,


01:26:56.480 --> 01:26:58.444
remember?


01:26:58.960 --> 01:27:02.119
I was there to comfort
Anita at the funeral.


01:27:02.120 --> 01:27:03.970
Such a sweet, innocent girl.


01:27:08.440 --> 01:27:10.688
Do you wanna do this here?


01:27:12.400 --> 01:27:14.887
Because one of us is on parole.


01:27:16.800 --> 01:27:19.526
But you know that, right?


01:27:27.840 --> 01:27:30.520
We'll settle this behind the wheel.


01:27:32.240 --> 01:27:34.479
I'm not worried about
you behind the wheel.


01:27:34.480 --> 01:27:36.205
Really?


01:27:37.000 --> 01:27:39.931
Why did you put a bounty on me?


01:27:41.160 --> 01:27:42.964
Tomorrow is gonna be fun.


01:27:43.560 --> 01:27:44.919
Yeah.


01:27:44.920 --> 01:27:48.519
When you're hanging
upside down tomorrow,


01:27:48.520 --> 01:27:50.370
I'm not coming back for you.


01:27:52.840 --> 01:27:55.281
Watch yourself, Tobey.


01:27:57.640 --> 01:27:59.365
See you tomorrow.


01:28:40.520 --> 01:28:42.927
You ran into him, didn't you?


01:28:45.320 --> 01:28:47.249
You need to forget about it.


01:28:48.000 --> 01:28:49.725
You need to let it go.


01:28:54.200 --> 01:28:55.879
I think you need to
get out of the car.


01:28:55.880 --> 01:28:59.129
And you need a hot shower,
and you need a good meal,


01:28:59.400 --> 01:29:03.321
and some rest, and some food.


01:29:04.800 --> 01:29:09.210
And I'm going to book
you a hotel room.


01:29:10.000 --> 01:29:14.250
No, I think it's best if you
just stay with me tonight.


01:29:20.880 --> 01:29:24.159
You know, it's just safer...


01:29:24.160 --> 01:29:25.600
If you stay with me.


01:29:30.520 --> 01:29:32.404
Right? Yeah.


01:29:47.280 --> 01:29:49.562
Look at you. Okay.


01:30:44.320 --> 01:30:45.965
Beast,


01:30:46.520 --> 01:30:47.919
we've been hit.


01:30:47.920 --> 01:30:49.759
All right, we're on our way.
We're on our way.


01:30:49.760 --> 01:30:51.199
- Track them.
- I'm on it.


01:30:51.200 --> 01:30:52.399
Where is he?


01:30:52.400 --> 01:30:54.360
He's up on California
and Mason. Make a left.


01:30:57.720 --> 01:30:59.081
Are you okay?


01:31:02.160 --> 01:31:07.082
Go. Before the cops get here, go.


01:31:08.640 --> 01:31:10.046
God!


01:31:22.640 --> 01:31:25.571
I got you. I got you.


01:31:25.880 --> 01:31:28.559
Units, be advised, getting
report of a vehicle roll-over.


01:31:28.560 --> 01:31:30.330
115 Nob Hill.


01:31:40.840 --> 01:31:42.879
Unit 1-David responding. Code 3.


01:31:42.880 --> 01:31:44.320
Holy shit.


01:31:44.920 --> 01:31:46.119
Open the door.
We gotta let them in.


01:31:46.120 --> 01:31:47.881
- We gotta make this quick.
- All right.


01:31:50.080 --> 01:31:52.879
Yo, we gotta move. Cops are coming.


01:31:52.880 --> 01:31:54.359
Came in over the scanner.
We gotta go!


01:31:54.360 --> 01:31:55.759
Come on, man.


01:31:55.760 --> 01:31:57.200
We gotta go.


01:31:58.840 --> 01:32:00.159
Tobey, you guys good?


01:32:00.160 --> 01:32:01.719
We need a hospital.


01:32:01.720 --> 01:32:04.121
- Find a hospital. Find a hospital.
- I'm working on it.


01:32:07.920 --> 01:32:10.327
All right, I got a hospital
on Hill. Make a left.


01:32:21.360 --> 01:32:24.040
Wait! We need your help.


01:32:30.480 --> 01:32:32.648
What's her name? Did she
ever lose consciousness?


01:32:32.960 --> 01:32:36.323
Julia. Yeah, she's been in and out.


01:32:36.480 --> 01:32:38.330
- You stay with her, all right?
- I will.


01:32:38.400 --> 01:32:40.523
- Take care of her.
- Come on. We gotta go.


01:32:42.640 --> 01:32:44.365
- Go, go, go.
- We're here.


01:33:45.200 --> 01:33:47.243
Anita,


01:33:49.120 --> 01:33:52.130
why don't you just leave him?


01:34:01.720 --> 01:34:03.888
I just did.


01:34:14.240 --> 01:34:17.559
I know that Dino was there
the night my brother died.


01:34:17.560 --> 01:34:20.570
Yeah. He was.


01:34:22.280 --> 01:34:24.642
I wish I could give you
those years back.


01:34:26.560 --> 01:34:28.599
Anita,


01:34:28.600 --> 01:34:30.848
I need a car.


01:34:51.400 --> 01:34:53.284
I'm sorry, Tobey.


01:34:55.600 --> 01:34:57.643
So am I.


01:36:00.840 --> 01:36:02.883
Why wouldn't he destroy it?


01:36:03.920 --> 01:36:05.565
I have no idea.


01:36:05.720 --> 01:36:09.720
I guess some people just don't
think they'll ever get caught.


01:36:49.840 --> 01:36:51.041
How is she?


01:36:52.560 --> 01:36:56.651
Arm is broke. Waiting
on the CAT scan.


01:37:46.600 --> 01:37:48.211
Hey.


01:37:51.280 --> 01:37:53.005
How you feeling?


01:37:59.440 --> 01:38:01.290
Beat up.


01:38:02.560 --> 01:38:04.808
But I'm fine.


01:38:09.120 --> 01:38:11.004
You know...


01:38:12.480 --> 01:38:14.682
You are not the girl
I thought you were.


01:38:15.080 --> 01:38:20.207
Well, you learn a lot about a person
when they've been hit by a truck.


01:38:29.240 --> 01:38:32.205
What are you gonna
do about tomorrow?


01:38:33.480 --> 01:38:35.762
I found a car.


01:38:38.160 --> 01:38:41.603
Do I wanna know where
you found the car?


01:38:42.080 --> 01:38:44.119
No, you don't.


01:38:44.120 --> 01:38:46.163
Is it fast?


01:38:46.800 --> 01:38:49.401
It's fast enough, yeah.


01:38:59.320 --> 01:39:01.204
Do it for Pete.


01:39:02.040 --> 01:39:03.730
What?


01:39:06.600 --> 01:39:10.122
This is for Pete.


01:39:17.520 --> 01:39:19.210
Yeah.


01:39:54.320 --> 01:39:57.919
This is, by far, the best De
Leon I've ever put together.


01:39:57.920 --> 01:40:01.283
This is my David, man.
This is my Pieta.


01:40:01.560 --> 01:40:03.649
This is my Soup Can.


01:40:11.240 --> 01:40:13.199
Is it possible to get a laptop?


01:40:13.200 --> 01:40:15.243
Sure. I'll be right back.


01:40:29.280 --> 01:40:31.881
Hey, what's up, baby?
What's your name?


01:40:33.480 --> 01:40:34.599
Right.


01:40:34.600 --> 01:40:38.282
Do you have an iPad
I can borrow? Please?


01:40:41.720 --> 01:40:42.959
We've got our lineup.


01:40:42.960 --> 01:40:45.322
Each driver takes his
spot at the starting line.


01:40:45.400 --> 01:40:48.199
In the first row is English
Paul in a Bugatti Veyron


01:40:48.200 --> 01:40:50.801
and Dino Brewster in his
Lamborghini Elemento.


01:40:51.000 --> 01:40:54.079
Row two is the Gooch
in a Saleen S7.


01:40:54.080 --> 01:40:56.679
Texas Mike is in the McLaren P1.


01:40:56.680 --> 01:41:00.168
The third row has Johnny
V in his GTA Spano.


01:41:01.360 --> 01:41:05.039
I'm looking at $7 million in cars


01:41:05.040 --> 01:41:08.403
and thousands of horsepower.
Winner takes all.


01:41:08.440 --> 01:41:11.564
Losers, y'all can walk home.


01:41:14.760 --> 01:41:16.279
No sign of Tobey Marshall.


01:41:16.280 --> 01:41:19.399
I don't really know what
all that's about, but I...


01:41:19.400 --> 01:41:21.443
Hold up. Wait, hold on.


01:41:27.360 --> 01:41:29.199
Wait a minute, now.


01:41:29.200 --> 01:41:32.802
A sixth car has just
arrived, but I can't...


01:41:44.880 --> 01:41:48.926
Tobey Marshall just stepped
out of a red Agera.


01:41:50.080 --> 01:41:52.726
Well! Maybe the
little tart was right


01:41:53.000 --> 01:41:58.081
about there being three
Koenigseggs the day Pete died.


01:42:19.840 --> 01:42:23.522
You like the car I brought?
Because I know the cops will.


01:42:25.560 --> 01:42:28.159
And by the way,


01:42:28.160 --> 01:42:30.931
I think this belongs to you.


01:43:45.080 --> 01:43:47.799
Tobey Marshall and Johnny
V are battling for fifth.


01:43:47.800 --> 01:43:49.400
You got it, you got it, you got it.


01:43:55.480 --> 01:43:57.079
And Johnny V is off the road.


01:43:57.080 --> 01:43:58.520
Come on, come on, come on!


01:44:40.840 --> 01:44:43.199
Golden Gate, this is H1.
I got ops on them.


01:44:43.200 --> 01:44:44.526
Westbound 128.


01:44:48.440 --> 01:44:51.928
Tobey Marshall's gonna roll the dice and
try to split the Saleen and the P1.


01:45:00.080 --> 01:45:01.439
- Yo, yo, yo.
- And he does it.


01:45:01.440 --> 01:45:02.959
Yo, that's my dude right
there. That's my dude.


01:45:02.960 --> 01:45:04.399
- Ladies and gentlemen...
- Y'all come check this out.


01:45:04.400 --> 01:45:06.599
Marshall's balls have
just been located


01:45:06.600 --> 01:45:09.239
and they are very, very large.


01:45:09.240 --> 01:45:13.399
Texas Mike in the McLaren is now
fifth, Tobey is now running fourth.


01:45:13.400 --> 01:45:16.843
Dino Brewster, you better
watch your ass, son.


01:45:23.240 --> 01:45:25.519
Suspects approaching
150 miles per hour.


01:45:25.520 --> 01:45:27.324
H1 will try to stall them.


01:45:27.560 --> 01:45:29.683
All units, 10-3.


01:45:31.960 --> 01:45:35.767
I've got flying cops. I've
got flies in the ointment.


01:45:35.880 --> 01:45:38.559
I got CHP in the air
all over the course.


01:45:38.560 --> 01:45:40.559
You add cops to the
race and people get...


01:45:40.560 --> 01:45:43.331
Racers should race,
cops should eat donuts.


01:46:04.320 --> 01:46:07.599
All units, disregard the spike strips.
They're moving too fast.


01:46:07.600 --> 01:46:08.759
They'll get past the
deployment spot.


01:46:08.760 --> 01:46:10.439
Let's try the rolling
block instead.


01:46:10.440 --> 01:46:11.679
18-4, roger?


01:46:11.680 --> 01:46:13.879
18-2, six on Code 3.


01:46:13.880 --> 01:46:16.287
Rolling block in formation, check.


01:46:55.920 --> 01:47:00.523
The Gooch in the Saleen has
been totally taken out.


01:47:00.760 --> 01:47:02.849
I can't believe what I'm seeing.


01:47:03.440 --> 01:47:06.519
British Paul holds first,
Dino is still in second,


01:47:06.520 --> 01:47:08.039
Tobey Marshall moves into third.


01:47:08.040 --> 01:47:09.519
Yeah, boy.


01:47:09.520 --> 01:47:11.131
All right, brother, keep it going.


01:47:11.960 --> 01:47:15.209
Dispatch, officers involved
in TC. I need rescue, now.


01:47:29.800 --> 01:47:32.241
All units, they TC'd into
two of our officers.


01:47:34.840 --> 01:47:38.599
Be advised, five suspect vehicles
are entering the tree line.


01:47:38.600 --> 01:47:41.039
Consider using lethal force.


01:47:41.040 --> 01:47:42.685
They're at mile marker 27.


01:48:43.280 --> 01:48:46.039
Dispatch, confirm rescue is rolling.
We have another officer down


01:48:46.040 --> 01:48:48.846
as well as another suspect.
18-5, are you set up for the pit?


01:48:49.120 --> 01:48:51.049
18-5 in position.


01:49:07.200 --> 01:49:09.079
Suspects approaching
on a five count.


01:49:09.080 --> 01:49:10.884
18-5, countdown begins.


01:49:13.800 --> 01:49:15.001
Five,


01:49:16.800 --> 01:49:18.001
four,


01:49:19.440 --> 01:49:20.641
three,


01:49:21.320 --> 01:49:22.681
two,


01:49:23.000 --> 01:49:24.201
on 8.


01:49:45.280 --> 01:49:47.926
18-5, perfect pit.
Lead suspect down.


01:49:48.040 --> 01:49:52.479
I'm hearing over scanners,
the Bugatti has just got taken out.


01:49:52.480 --> 01:49:54.330
Man. Wait a minute...


01:49:54.880 --> 01:49:58.399
Wait a minute, Tobey Marshall has
somehow just taken the lead.


01:49:58.400 --> 01:50:01.604
Dino Brewster is running
last in third place?


01:50:02.000 --> 01:50:04.601
- Are you kidding me?
- Hold that lead! Hold that lead!


01:50:05.480 --> 01:50:07.045
And then there were three.


01:50:07.280 --> 01:50:09.448
We need containment set
at Navarro Bridge.


01:50:21.560 --> 01:50:25.810
H1, Mendo PD is Code
3 to Navarro Bridge.


01:50:31.440 --> 01:50:33.559
They're coming up to the
race marker to the bridge.


01:50:33.560 --> 01:50:36.039
Tobey is clearly running first.
I can't believe it.


01:50:36.040 --> 01:50:39.719
The blue collar kid from Mount Kisco is
trying to wear Cinderella's slipper.


01:50:39.720 --> 01:50:42.241
That's my dude!
Mount Kisco, let's go!


01:50:57.280 --> 01:51:01.039
By the way, these cop cars,
they top out at about 130.


01:51:01.040 --> 01:51:03.004
Hold them back, baby!
Hold them back.


01:51:03.040 --> 01:51:05.846
Good luck catching up, Smokey.
I'll tell you who wins.


01:51:36.840 --> 01:51:38.326
Come on!


01:52:02.120 --> 01:52:03.879
Dispatch, another suspect is down.


01:52:03.880 --> 01:52:05.684
Only two remaining.


01:52:09.440 --> 01:52:12.450
The Elemento just flicked
the P1 into a roll.


01:52:12.480 --> 01:52:16.571
We're down to Tobey
Marshall and Dino Brewster.


01:52:18.240 --> 01:52:19.965
This ain't just about racing.


01:52:50.520 --> 01:52:53.200
Don't do it. Tobey,
don't let him do it.


01:53:19.320 --> 01:53:21.999
Tobey Marshall just let
the Elemento get by him.


01:53:22.000 --> 01:53:23.319
- Nice move.
- That kid better wake up.


01:53:23.320 --> 01:53:24.759
Wake up, Toby!


01:53:24.760 --> 01:53:29.409
Wake up and smell that $2
million Lambo in your pocket.


01:54:01.920 --> 01:54:05.090
Don't do it, brother. It's not
worth it. You can beat him.


01:54:10.800 --> 01:54:13.651
Pete... I need you, pal.


01:54:23.440 --> 01:54:24.801
Okay, let's go.


01:54:58.360 --> 01:55:03.009
Jeez, Dino took a swing and
missed and flipped the Elemento.


01:55:03.720 --> 01:55:07.039
Dino Brewster is out.
Down goes Dino!


01:55:07.040 --> 01:55:09.559
Thank you, thank you, thank you!


01:55:09.560 --> 01:55:12.599
Tobey is the last man standing!
He's gonna win the De Leon!


01:55:12.600 --> 01:55:14.279
He's gonna win the De Leon!


01:55:14.280 --> 01:55:17.559
The Marshall kid from Mount Kisco!
He's gonna make a milk run to victory!


01:55:17.560 --> 01:55:19.959
That's right! That's my boy!
That's my dude!


01:55:19.960 --> 01:55:21.919
That's right. Give me space.
I'm about to twerk it out.


01:55:21.920 --> 01:55:23.319
Tobey is the last man standing!


01:55:23.320 --> 01:55:26.039
- Get it. Hit it, hit it.
- He's gonna win the De Leon!


01:55:26.040 --> 01:55:27.759
I can't believe what I'm seeing!


01:55:27.760 --> 01:55:31.009
The kid from Mount Kisco!
The blue collar kid!


01:55:48.720 --> 01:55:50.559
Wait! Wait.


01:55:50.560 --> 01:55:51.839
What are you doing?


01:55:51.840 --> 01:55:53.800
- What are you doing?
- Why are you stopping?


01:56:19.760 --> 01:56:21.724
Come on. Come on.


01:56:23.880 --> 01:56:25.320
Come on.


01:56:31.440 --> 01:56:32.999
Hey, you okay?


01:56:33.000 --> 01:56:36.283
Yeah. I'm fine.


01:56:39.080 --> 01:56:40.486
I'm fine.


01:56:40.800 --> 01:56:43.162
Good. This is for Pete.


01:58:10.520 --> 01:58:12.210
Let me see your hands!


01:58:17.760 --> 01:58:19.199
Let me see your hands!


01:58:19.200 --> 01:58:20.481
Now!


01:59:03.400 --> 01:59:05.921
Stand up! Keep your hands
where I can see them.


01:59:06.440 --> 01:59:10.239
18-7, Euro plates
Sam-Mary-Harry, 2-2-8,


01:59:10.240 --> 01:59:12.119
registered to a Dino Brewster.


01:59:12.120 --> 01:59:14.482
Well, now, hold on, cretins.


01:59:15.160 --> 01:59:18.199
I'm hearing over the
scanners that the Koenigsegg


01:59:18.200 --> 01:59:20.359
does indeed belong to Dino


01:59:20.360 --> 01:59:22.767
and that's the missing
evidence that killed Pete.


01:59:25.120 --> 01:59:27.399
Well, then it looks
like Dino, Dino bambino


01:59:27.400 --> 01:59:30.683
is going away for a
long, long time.


02:00:17.760 --> 02:00:20.439
Well, kiddos, it looks
like Tobey himself


02:00:20.440 --> 02:00:22.679
is gonna enjoy three hots
and a cot in the pokey


02:00:22.680 --> 02:00:24.689
for illegal street racing.


02:00:26.680 --> 02:00:27.927
I don't know, Tobey.


02:00:29.120 --> 02:00:31.800
A few months in jail to
prove your innocence.


02:00:33.680 --> 02:00:35.644
Was it worth it, kid?


02:01:11.000 --> 02:01:12.770
All right. Step forward.


02:02:00.200 --> 02:02:01.925
Get in!


02:02:02.120 --> 02:02:03.845
I'll drive.


02:02:03.920 --> 02:02:06.851
I've seen you drive
and it's terrifying.


02:02:11.760 --> 02:02:13.371
Come on, lovebirds.


02:02:13.760 --> 02:02:15.399
We need to get Benny
out of the clink.


02:02:15.400 --> 02:02:17.359
Maverick is getting out
for good behavior.


02:02:17.360 --> 02:02:19.599
Yeah, apparently he started
some fitness program


02:02:19.600 --> 02:02:21.119
for the inmates or some shit.


02:02:21.120 --> 02:02:22.810
We got five hours to get to Utah.


02:02:22.920 --> 02:02:24.201
Let's go.


02:02:54.760 --> 02:02:56.399
Yeah.


02:02:56.400 --> 02:02:58.399
Yeah, that's right, baby.


02:02:58.400 --> 02:02:59.999
You're rocking with the champ.


02:03:00.000 --> 02:03:02.279
You're rocking with the champ.
Number one.


02:03:02.280 --> 02:03:05.199
Don't even call me Maverick no more.
Call me Benny the Champ.


02:03:05.200 --> 02:03:07.479
That's right, baby. That's good,
Jeff. I see you, Jeff.


02:03:07.480 --> 02:03:10.479
What are you doing?
What are you doing, Gerald?


02:03:10.480 --> 02:03:11.799
Twerk!


02:03:11.800 --> 02:03:14.079
You know what? You got a solo.
Come on over here.


02:03:14.080 --> 02:03:16.679
Let's see the solo, bro.
Let's see the solo.


02:03:16.680 --> 02:03:19.451
Get it, Gerald! Get it, bro!


02:03:22.040 --> 02:03:24.004
That's what I'm talking
about, bro! Yes!
